{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('TASK.md')\nfor i,line in enumerate(p.read_text().splitlines(),1):\n    if line.startswith(('Source', '## ', 'Attract', 'Multiplayer', 'Scope', '- How', '- What', '- Did', '- If', '- Date', '- Source:', '- Plan:', '- Usage:')):\n        print(f'{i}: {line}')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('TASK.md')\nfor i,line in enumerate(p.read_text().splitlines(),1):\n    if line.startswith(('Source', '## ', 'Attract', 'Multiplayer', 'Scope', '- How', '- What', '- Did', '- If', '- Date', '- Source:', '- Plan:', '- Usage:')):\n        print(f'{i}: {line}')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"32: ## This computer\n65: ## Goal\n69: Scope\n75: Attract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n77: Multiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n81: ## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\n88: ## Done\n91: ## Source Information\n93: - Date: 2026-11-06 02:12:10\n94: - Source: the work it's based on\n95: - Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n106: - Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n131: - How many issues did testing catch?\n132: - How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n133: - What was the most helpful test you ran?\n134: - What was the least helpful test you ran?\n138: - What did you like most about the engine?\n139: - Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n140: - What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n141: - What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n142: - What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n143: - If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n147: - What did you like most about this prompt?\n148: - What was confusing?\n149: - What was the hardest thing to do?\n150: - What would you change in this prompt?\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
