search/hub/README.md:71:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:74:- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:77:- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:78:- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:83:- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:111:- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:114:- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the game has loaded and the round can\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:127:| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:143:AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:198:- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:200:  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:208:- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:210:  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:211:  `finish()` by then is void.\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:218:| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:240:- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:244:`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:249:- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:252:Places and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:273:- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:286:- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:287:- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:301:  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:326:python3 -m http.server 8000\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:333:`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:345:- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:366:| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:367:| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:368:| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:369:| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:370:| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:371:| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:379:| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:380:| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:386:| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:401:| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:402:| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:412:protocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"The engine and Hub interfaces are verified. I’ll build the plan around a ten-bout solo tour, local versus, and a short Hub match using the same combat rules. The added depth will come from destructible castle layouts, distinct stone shots, and readable AI opponents. I’ll also flag the source’s disputed release year and leave the title and output naming to each builder’s brief.\n"}}
