{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'TODO|placeholder|unknown|first script|active|server|seats|cancel|timeout|90-second|three-minute|below|142|artifacts|UI scale|1.05M' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"3:Builder: **gpt-6.1-sol ultracode, 1.05M context window**. Use that capacity to carry the complete game design, engine contracts, content definitions, network lifecycle, and test evidence together thro [... omitted end of long line]\n5:Your own CEO brief controls the source label, output naming, development directory, run metadata, and required reporting. Choose the game's title yourself: privately generate 50 playful riffs on the s [... omitted end of long line]\n28:Stone Sling and Smithereens! are regional names for the source. No source campaign, elaborate enemy roster, independent aiming-angle system, or wind mechanic was established. The solo tour, special st [... omitted end of long line]\n51:**Hub Versus:** exactly two players in a shared authoritative world. Use a compact, self-contained match on one court, bounded at three minutes, with the same stones, destruction, recovery, and scorin [... omitted end of long line]\n53:**Attract mode:** after exactly ten seconds without meaningful input on the standalone title/front-menu screens, play a looping demonstration using the real simulation. Any input exits and is consumed [... omitted end of long line]\n62:- Hold Fire to build tension from zero to full; release to launch. The meter stops at full rather than silently wrapping. A maximum-power shot normally overshoots useful targets, so precision remains  [... omitted end of long line]\n64:- Reload is automatic, initially about 0.9 seconds for the ordinary stone. A buffered press may begin the next charge when reloading completes; releasing before it can begin cancels the buffer. Never  [... omitted end of long line]\n78:Different launch-speed curves are allowed, but keep all required targets reachable and show a separate remembered range marker per stone type. Do not simulate weight by applying inconsistent gravity.  [... omitted end of long line]\n86:- On either interruption, cancel any pending charge and clear its input latch. Do not queue a shot for the returning unit.\n101:Destroy all objective blocks to win a battle. Resolve all impacts scheduled for the same simulation tick before adjudicating: mutual destruction in that tick is a draw. An ordinary bout has a visible  [... omitted end of long line]\n107:Build five genuinely different court compositions from reusable materials and rules. Layouts affect shot selection and target exposure; changing only the sky color does not make a new court. Keep both [... omitted end of long line]\n147:Compose for TV first: show the lane and highest useful trajectory with safe margins for HUD and overscan. Preserve a clear aiming silhouette at the farthest useful distance. On narrower displays, fit  [... omitted end of long line]\n171:| Pause | Options | Escape when not cancelling a live charge |\n173:Resolve cancel versus pause clearly: first Escape/Circle cancels an active charge; a subsequent pause action opens the pause menu. If testing finds this unclear, give cancel a separate binding and kee [... omitted end of long line]\n175:Keyboard/mouse must feel native. Mouse position chooses an intended world target/range reference, and a hover highlights the target under it; holding and releasing fires by the same tension rule as a  [... omitted end of long line]\n181:Touch gameplay needs only the menu affordance persistently visible. Hold a thumb anywhere in the friendly half/bottom firing region to wind; release to fire. Show a temporary tension halo at contact a [... omitted end of long line]\n183:Settings include music/effects/voice, glyph family, controls/rebinding, charge tension, prediction assist, reduced motion, and comfortable TV UI scale. Persist them defensively. Pausing solo/local pla [... omitted end of long line]\n221:  input.js                   seats, device adapters, safe cancellation\n230:artifacts/                   generated verification evidence and build staging\n233:Keep the structure useful rather than ceremonially creating an empty file for each row. JavaScript ES modules and a small Node-based bundler are sufficient; use another language/tool only when it mate [... omitted end of long line]\n237:Use stable IDs and serializable state. A useful snapshot includes tick, seed, mode/phase, court/bout, players, selected stones, charge/reload/recovery endpoints, active projectiles, changed castle blo [... omitted end of long line]\n251:1. Embed the released Hub client **verbatim**, as the first script in the final HTML head immediately after charset. Keep game code outside that script; the Hub recognizes and upgrades unmodified rele [... omitted end of long line]\n252:2. Declare protocol `1`, `hub:session-players` as `2-2`, mode `shared-world`, a short goal/how-to, and the three-minute round declaration. Keep declaration and `AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', s [... omitted end of long line]\n253:3. Check `AIHub.active` before starting standalone menus, attract mode, or saved-tour resume. Active sessions bypass all of them. A `null` connection result is the documented standalone fallback.\n256:6. The host owns physics, projectile creation, all damage/collapse, RNG, scores, timers, disconnections, and outcomes. Each client renders confirmed state and sends intentions. A separate `AIHub.serve [... omitted end of long line]\n264:Send sequence-numbered charge-begin, release/cancel, and stone-choice intentions reliably to the host. Identify the player from the event's authenticated `from` value, never from a claimed seat in a p [... omitted end of long line]\n268:Use host snapshots at a modest rate, initially around 6–8 per second, plus reliable launch/impact/collapse/recovery/outcome events. Interpolate only presentation. Enforce the **aggregate** outgoing bu [... omitted end of long line]\n284:- Restart current bout, choose court/bout/opponent, skip teaching, switch AI/human seats, restore castles, clear projectiles, and force a result for presentation inspection.\n293:Provide one command, **`npm run verify`**, for all meaningful automated verification. It exits nonzero on failure and prints only failure details plus a final one-line count such as `142 checks, 0 fai [... omitted end of long line]\n302:| Charge/input | Short/medium/full holds, legal cancel, buffered reload, mixed-device ownership, independent two-player holds/releases, focus loss/disconnect, pointer cancellation, no duplicate fire | [... omitted end of long line]\n305:| Match/tour | Win, loss, draw, timeout tie ordering, exactly-once result; weighted banked totals; all ten bouts and five courts; save/resume; final ceremony and replay |\n312:| Hub | Two independent players; no-local-player server; loss/jitter/reorder; host leave/player leave; time-up; valid standings; packet budget; consistent block state; no startup input required |\n316:Use the official Hub harness and its required sibling files over a loopback server on an **OS-selected** port. Confirm the served page is your built game before trusting results. Required cases includ [... omitted end of long line]\n327:2. **Prove the shared combat contract.** Implement fixed-station simultaneous charge/release, one stone, a genuinely destructible castle, crew/launcher interruptions and protection, and deterministic  [... omitted end of long line]\n332:7. **Package and close.** Build the single-file artifact, verify it independently via `file://` and the Hub harness, validate metadata/interview schemas and naming against your own brief, remove devel [... omitted end of long line]\n340:No runtime request may depend on a development module, neighboring file, local server, absolute workstation path, or untracked asset. External CDN dependencies are permitted by the brief, but none is  [... omitted end of long line]\n342:All generated development files, harness copies, browser evidence, dependency stores under project control, and build staging stay in your own folder. Publish only the requested artifacts to the locat [... omitted end of long line]\n344:About/Credits and the final chat reply must contain **Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback**. Maintain one metadata source to prevent contradictions between game, [... omitted end of long line]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('PLAN.md')\ns=p.read_text()\na=json.loads(Path('planner-exit-interview.json').read_text())\nexpected=[\n'What did you like most about this prompt?',\n'What was confusing?',\n'What was the hardest thing to do?',\n'What would you change in this prompt?',\n]\nassert isinstance(a,list) and len(a)==4\nfor row,q in zip(a,expected):\n    assert set(row)=={'question','answer'}\n    assert row['question']==q\n    assert isinstance(row['answer'],str) and row['answer'].strip()\nassert s.count('\"'```'\"') % 2 == 0\nfor forbidden in ['20261106-021210', '/home/micha/', '[GameTitle', 'planner-exit-interview.json', 'exit-interview.json']:\n    assert forbidden not in s, forbidden\nprint(f'PLAN.md: {len(s.split())} words, {len(s.splitlines())} lines')\nprint('Planner interview: valid JSON, four exact questions, nonempty answers')\nprint('Plan naming and relative-path checks passed')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
