{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '255,303p' .planner-research/hub/README.md && sed -n '400,463p' .planner-research/hub/session.js\"","aggregated_output":"\n## Sending data between copies\n\n### Parallel\n\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n\n### Ghost\n\nEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\nthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\nonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\ncharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n\n### Shared world\n\n- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n  every copy.\n\n### `send()` and `message`\n\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n  client drops the rest.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\nIn a session:\n\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\n   */\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\n      return null;\n    }\n    var copy = {};\n    for (var key in outcome) {\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\n    }\n    return copy;\n  }\n\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    var given = outcome || {};\n    delete fields.time;\n    delete fields.score;\n    if (finite(given.time)) fields.time = Number(given.time);\n    if (finite(given.score)) fields.score = Number(given.score);\n    if (!own(fields, 'time') && !own(fields, 'score')) return warn('result needs a finite time or score');\n    reported = true;\n    if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n    post('result', fields);\n  };\n\n  /** Versus and co-op: the host reports the standings once, best first, ties grouped: [[2], [0, 3], [1]]. */\n  hub.finish = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    if (!hub.isHost) return warn('finish is for the host only');\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    if (!Array.isArray(fields.standings)) return warn('finish needs standings');\n    reported = true;\n    post('finish', fields);\n  };\n\n  function sendProgress() {\n    progressTimer = null;\n    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\n    lastProgress = now();\n    post('progress', nextProgress);\n    nextProgress = null;\n  }\n\n  /** Your standing during play, for the hub's scoreboard: {score, label}. Call it as often as you like; the hub hears it about once a second. */\n  hub.progress = function (p) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported || !p || !finite(p.score)) return;\n    nextProgress = { score: Number(p.score) };\n    if (p.label != null) nextProgress.label = String(p.label).slice(0, 24);\n    var wait = lastProgress + PROGRESS_EVERY_MS - now();\n    if (wait <= 0) sendProgress();\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'hitFx\\\\(|explosion\\\\(|freeze:|send =|function send|return false|ack|both ways|both directions|traffic|auto.play|Arrow' .planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js .planner-research/hub/session.js .planner-research/hub/harness.html .planner-research/hub/README.md\"","aggregated_output":".planner-research/hub/README.md:165:  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:291:  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n.planner-research/hub/README.md:343:- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:11:  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 14px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; }\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:13:  header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:16:  input, select, button { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); background: #241f31; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; }\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:23:  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:24:  .cell__bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 3px 8px; background: var(--panel); font-size: 12px; }\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:27:  .cell iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; background: #000; }\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:29:  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); }\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:215:    label.innerHTML = `<span class=\"cell__dot\" style=\"background:${color}\"></span><b></b><span class=\"cell__state\"></span>`;\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:286:/** A player answered on the game's own card: Ready, or more time (+10 s; again takes it back). */\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:396:  if (!doc || !win) return false;\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:457:    const arrows = ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'a', 'd', 'w', 's'];\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:483:        check('parallel: no game traffic', state.cells.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent === 0),\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:492:      check('game traffic flows both ways', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0 && c.bridge.stats.received > 0) || n === 1,\n.planner-research/hub/harness.html:523:    check('harness ran', false, String(error?.stack || error));\n.planner-research/hub/session.js:327:  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n.planner-research/hub/session.js:352:  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n.planner-research/hub/session.js:353:    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\n.planner-research/hub/session.js:360:      return false;\n.planner-research/hub/session.js:362:    if (text === undefined) return false;\n.planner-research/hub/session.js:365:      return false;\n.planner-research/hub/session.js:372:      return false;\n.planner-research/hub/session.js:449:  function sendProgress() {\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:24: *      background (r.sky, map.drawFloor or level.draw) -> decals (ground marks, shadows)\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:50: *    new E.Backdrop('castle-night') behind levels, textured tiles (stone, brick, wood,\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:54: *    px.glow(g, 1) inside queue callbacks, pass { color, shadow } to lights.add, and\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:55: *    register shadow casters with game.lights.caster(). Falls back to Canvas lighting.\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:58: *    plays it back headless, exactly, and stops where it differs (game.stateHash = () => [...] sharpens that).\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:80:/** version: the release (package.json, written everywhere by node tools/version.mjs); build: the commit this copy was built\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:100:/** easing curves for u 0..1: linear, outQuad, inQuad, inOut (inOutQuad), outCubic, outBack (it overshoots a little more\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:101: *  than Penner's: 1.9), and the rest of Penner's set (sine, quad, cubic, back, elastic and bounce, each in, out and\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:109:  outBack: u => { const c1 = 1.9, c3 = c1 + 1; return 1 + c3 * Math.pow(u - 1, 3) + c1 * Math.pow(u - 1, 2); }   // overshoots past 1, then settles: pop-ups, landings\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:142:const CSS_NAMES = { black: '000', white: 'fff', red: 'f00', lime: '0f0', green: '008000', blue: '00f', yellow: 'ff0', cyan: '0ff', aqua: '0ff', magenta: 'f0f', fuchsia: 'f0f', gray: '808080', grey: '8 [... omitted end of long line]\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:307:const STORE_MEM = new Map(), memGet = (k, fallback) => STORE_MEM.has(k) ? JSON.parse(STORE_MEM.get(k)) : fallback;   // (the visit's values, where storage is missing, blocked or full)\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:311:  get(key, fallback = null) { const k = 'my3d2dge:' + key; try { const v = localStorage.getItem(k); if (v !== null) return JSON.parse(v); } catch (e) { return memGet(k, fallback); } return memGet(k, f [... omitted end of long line]\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:312:  set(key, value) { const k = 'my3d2dge:' + key, v = JSON.stringify(value); try { localStorage.setItem(k, v); STORE_MEM.delete(k); return true; } catch (e) { STORE_MEM.set(k, v); return false; } },    [... omitted end of long line]\n.planner-research/engine/my-3d2dge.js:339:  in